Notes: 
-----
At the start of each simulation session,
initialise the following environment variables:
For example..

# Set the peripheral path environment variable
setenv PERIPH /home/nbray/sfwork/snowdon/dcdc_pl160

# Set up peripheral specific data variables
setenv PERIPHERAL Dcdc
setenv PRODUCT PL160

set prompt = `hostname`':'`whoami`':PERIPH> '
# Set the technology library path environment variable

# For VHDL gate level simulations use Avant! CB25 VITAL
setenv LIB_VITAL $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/vhdl
# For Verilog gate level simulations use Avant! CB25 Verilog
setenv LIB_VERILOG $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/verilog
setenv LIB_UDP $PERIPH/../cb25/v2.1/verilog
setenv CELL_LIB CB25

The recommended method is to create a file, SourceMe, in dcdc_pl160 directory,
containing the above commands, and run UNIX source SourceMe.
The directory paths above need amending for each specific installation.

Simulations can setup to be executed via the makefile (UNIX make utility)
but change of cell library requires amendment to paths for netlist simulations.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Steps for running TicTalk Verilog simulations. 

Clock Enabled Tests - (Production)
----------------------------------
1. VERILOG RTL simulations
--------------------------

- Ensure that the Dcdc_prod.sim has been copied to
  TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.sim
  (Note that the Dcdc_prod.sim file should be generated from the BusTalk
  source file, Dcdc_prod.c, residing in the BusTalk/bustests directory
  as per the instructions in the README file in the same directory.)

- Additionally verify that a link exists from TicTalk/vlog/tbench/infile.sim
  to TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.sim.

  For simulations using the ModelSim simulator
  --------------------------------------------
  - In the TicTalk/vlog/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
    so that the library 'uut' points to the VERILOG RTL
    uut = $PERIPH/verilog/uut/work

  - Do a 'make clean' in the dcdc_pl160/verilog/uut directory

  - Do a 'make clean' in the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory
    (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following files:
      In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory  : vlog ticbox.v)

  - In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory, run simulations using
    vsim -lic_vlog tb_tic
    or
    make vsim_rtl

  - Use of the startup file (init.do) allows ModelSim to generate
    a toggle coverage report.

  For simulations using the Verilog-XL simulator
  ----------------------------------------------
  - In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory, run simulations using
    verilog +licq_vxl -f vxl.rtl tb_tic.v
    or
    make vxl_rtl

2. VERILOG NETLIST simulations
------------------------------

- Ensure that the Dcdc_prod.sim has been copied to
  TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.sim
  (Note that the Dcdc_prod.sim file should be generated from the BusTalk
  source file, Dcdc_prod.c, residing in the BusTalk/bustests directory
  as per the instructions in the README file in the same directory.)

- Additionally verify that a link exists from TicTalk/vlog/tbench/infile.sim
  to TicTalk/tictests/invec/infile.sim.

  For simulations using the ModelSim simulator
  --------------------------------------------
  - In the TicTalk/vlog/modeltech directory edit file 'libmap'
    so that the library 'uut' points to the VERILOG NETLIST
    uut = $PERIPH/verilog/uutNetlist/work

  - Do a 'make clean' in the dcdc_pl160/verilog/uutNetlist directory

  - Do a 'make clean' in the TicTalk/vlog directory
    (Alternatively one can selectively compile the following files:
      In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory  : vlog ticbox.v)

  - In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory, run simulations using
    vsim -lic_vlog \
      -sdfmax u_easy/u_rps/uDcdc=../../../verilog/uutNetlist/Dcdc_Verilog.sdf21 \
      -L UDP -L libverilog tb_tic
    vsim -lic_vlog \
      -sdfmin u_easy/u_rps/uDcdc=../../../verilog/uutNetlist/Dcdc_Verilog.sdf21 \
      -L UDP -L libverilog tb_tic
    or
    make vsim_net_max
    make vsim_net_min

  For simulations using the Verilog-XL simulator
  ----------------------------------------------
  - In the TicTalk/vlog/tbench directory, run simulations using

    verilog +define+NET_MAX \
    +licq_vxl +neg_tchk +libext+.v \
    -y ../sys -y ../chip ../tbench/ticbox.v \
    -y $LIB_VERILOG -y $LIB_UDP -v $LIB_UDP/mtb_verilog.v \
    ../../../verilog/uutNetlist/Dcdc_net.v \
    tb_tic.v
    verilog +define+NET_MIN \
    +licq_vxl +neg_tchk +libext+.v \
    -y ../sys -y ../chip ../tbench/ticbox.v \
    -y $LIB_VERILOG -y $LIB_UDP -v $LIB_UDP/mtb_verilog.v \
    ../../../verilog/uutNetlist/Dcdc_net.v \
    tb_tic.v
    or
    verilog +licq_vxl +define+NET_MAX -f vxl.net tb_tic.v
    verilog +licq_vxl +define+NET_MIN -f vxl.net tb_tic.v
    or
    make vxl_net_max_cb25
    make vxl_net_min_cb25

#-------------------------------------- End ------------------------------------
